---
description: Design tokens, typography, and visual direction
alwaysApply: true
---

Brand feel: slow living, tea estate mist, colonial heritage, wood-fired warmth. Quiet, premium, unhurried.

Tokens (define in Tailwind config / CSS vars):
- --mist: #DCE5DA (misty green)
- --tea: #2F4A3A (deep tea green)
- --cream: #F4EDE1
- --ember: #D9622B
- --char: #1A1714 (charcoal)
- --bark: #6B4A2F (accent brown)

Type:
- Display: a refined serif (Fraunces, Cormorant Garamond, or similar). Large, light weight, tight tracking.
- Body: clean sans (DM Sans or Manrope). Never Inter, Arial, or system default.
- Headlines huge on desktop (clamp 3.5rem to 9rem), generous line spacing on body.

Rules:
- Lots of whitespace. One idea per viewport.
- Full-bleed imagery, minimal borders and shadows, no cards-with-drop-shadows look.
- No purple/blue gradients, no glassmorphism, no emoji in UI, no stock "hero with two buttons" layout.
- Buttons: pill, subtle, magnetic hover. Primary = ember on dark, tea on light.
- Copy tone: warm, short, unpretentious. No marketing buzzwords.
- Sticky bar (WhatsApp / Call / Directions) on every viewport, bottom on mobile, side or top on desktop.
- Minimum tap target 44px. Contrast AA on all text.
